{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future","id":1211302,"title":"OPP, VtM 5E, and the Future","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-24T22:42:53-07:00","id":1211302,"title":"OPP, VtM 5E, and the Future","content":"With V5 going up for preorder soon, what is the future of OPP's license with Vampire: the Masquerade, and the rest of the WoD? If OPP continues with the current WoD, will they be in conjunction with V5, or if not continuing with the metaplot of V5, will they just work with the V4 material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T23:51:52-07:00","id":1211310,"title":"","content":"We still have a number of World of Darkness projects in the works, and that hasn't changed with V5. Rich has covered on the Monday Meeting blog earlier that White Wolf has encouraged us to submit pitches for V5 supplements. Our license hasn't changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T01:34:39-07:00","id":1211322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future#post1211302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With V5 going up for preorder soon, what is the future of OPP's license with Vampire: the Masquerade, and the rest of the WoD? If OPP continues with the current WoD, will they be in conjunction with V5, or if not continuing with the metaplot of V5, will they just work with the V4 material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on my memory from the recording of nuWW's Gencon 2017 panel...<br /> <br /> <u>Nu-White Wolf is <b>NOT</b> developing every single WoD5e book in-house.</u><br /> <br /> This is because nuWW is more of a licensing company and not quite a straight RPG developer company. Stuff like the VtM5e corebook and the Guide to the [Sect] 5e books will be directly developed by nu-WW (even then I'm not sure about the mentioned 5e Sabbat book). Everything else though is up in the air. So theoretical 5e versions of the clanbooks, the Player's Guide, the Storyteller's Guide, [City] by Night books, Ghoul book, etc could be developed by a different RPG company that's not nuWW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T14:25:15-07:00","id":1211564,"title":"","content":"What my major concern is: that nu-WW will require major changes to all future 4E books that OPP already has in the works, and that V5 will be a colossal shitbrick.<br /> <br /> I'm very reserved on how i feel about nu-WW's changes. I guess that's why I was never a fan of CofD.....too different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","user":"Japheth","date":". 04-25-2018, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T14:33:00-07:00","id":1211568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1211564#post1211564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What my major concern is: that nu-WW will require major changes to all future 4E books that OPP already has in the works, and that V5 will be a colossal shitbrick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd say that jury's out on that. Since the last major change was in Wraith20...and all that turned out to be was just requests for changes in length of the section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess that's why I was never a fan of CofD.....too different. </div> </div> </div>...except Chronicles of Darkness, back when it was still New World of Darkness, preceded Paradox's buyout by several years...?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:01:25-07:00","id":1213904,"title":"","content":"Different people behind the respective new versions does not rule out them having a similar quality/relationship to the existing gameline that people might take exception to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:21:47-07:00","id":1214289,"title":"","content":"I made the leap and did the preorder for the V5 neonate bumble (consisting of the corebook and 20 dice) at the price of $68.99. But beware.... because its going to be shipped from the UK, they tack on an additional $40 in shipping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:26:31-07:00","id":1214293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1211568#post1211568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I'd say that jury's out on that. Since the last major change was in Wraith20...and all that turned out to be was just requests for changes in length of the section.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...except Chronicles of Darkness, back when it was still New World of Darkness, preceded Paradox's buyout by several years...?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am fully aware that nWoD preceded Paradox's buyout..... in fact, it preceded CCP purchasing WW. However, I still maintain that I'm dubious on whether V5 will be even compatible with the previous four editions of VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:45:17-07:00","id":1214302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214293#post1214293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am fully aware that nWoD preceded Paradox's buyout..... in fact, it preceded CCP purchasing WW.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you knew that, why did you bring it up to begin with as if it were related?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I still maintain that I'm dubious on whether V5 will be even compatible with the previous four editions of VtM. </div> </div> </div>...compatible how...?<br /> <br /> Mechanics wise...yeah it's been known they're overhauling a bunch of things, whether people like them or not. Setting and story wise...well, they were reportedly happy enough with BJD to let it move forward to release. It would be strange if they retconned all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:44:18-07:00","id":1214402,"title":"","content":"Crowley here. got a couple of questions about V5<br /> <br /> Does anyone knows if is set Before, After or During Gehenna?<br /> <br /> can i sell one of my kidneys for the game? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:32:33-07:00","id":1214546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214402#post1214402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crowley here. got a couple of questions about V5<br /> <br /> Does anyone knows if is set Before, After or During Gehenna?<br /> <br /> can i sell one of my kidneys for the game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supposedly during Gehenna. However, as it is outlined in BJD, Gehenna is a cyclical thing.<br /> <br /> As for selling one of your kidneys.... Since the cost of shipping it is almost as expensive as the book itself, its up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:37:11-07:00","id":1214547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214302#post1214302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you knew that, why did you bring it up to begin with as if it were related?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I brought it up because I disliked nWoD tremendously, and also because I am hoping that they (nu-WW) don't make a drastic change to the system, similar to nWoD when WW originally published VtR, and to me it is relatable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:44:30-07:00","id":1214596,"title":"","content":"It looks compatible enough. If an old stat sheet gives an NPC four dots in Fortitude etc you can still use it even if the specifics of Fortitude has changed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T08:54:57-07:00","id":1214627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214547#post1214547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I brought it up because I disliked nWoD tremendously, and also because I am hoping that they (nu-WW) don't make a drastic change to the system, similar to nWoD when WW originally published VtR, and to me it is relatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>...you mean the gameline that was supposed to be its own separate thing unconnected to the original WoD, was never meant to be VtM4e to begin with, that people misread completely?<br /> <br /> Not seeing the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:50:09-07:00","id":1214702,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a>: Since you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar997_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"997\" data-vbnamecard=\"997\">Japheth</a> seem to be talking past each other, what I gather from the way that post #4 was written is that V5 reminds him of when Requiem came out with the massive changes in rules, such as touchstones, blood potency, and the huge rewrite of a number of disciplines, which is being mirrored with much of what I, at least, know of V5.<br /> <br /> Granted, I haven't been following V5 very closely, only what I've found on these fora, so I'm not privy to everything, and I'm wary of V5 as well, for many of the same reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:47:05-07:00","id":1214837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214702#post1214702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a>: Since you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar997_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"997\" data-vbnamecard=\"997\">Japheth</a> seem to be talking past each other, what I gather from the way that post #4 was written is that V5 reminds him of when Requiem came out with the massive changes in rules, such as touchstones, blood potency, and the huge rewrite of a number of disciplines, which is being mirrored with much of what I, at least, know of V5.<br /> <br /> Granted, I haven't been following V5 very closely, only what I've found on these fora, so I'm not privy to everything, and I'm wary of V5 as well, for many of the same reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which even then, I'd say it's still not comparable due to intent.<br /> <br /> VtR (and subsequently the rest of nWoD/CofD) was meant to be a brand new gameline separate from the original WoD. Inspired by it, sure, but still a different gameline. The gameline was not and has never been Vampire the Masquerade 4th Edition, it was Vampire the Requiem. So to expect it to be almost exactly the same as VtMRev or to be as a follow up to it I feel was not the right mindset to make.<br /> <br /> Conversely, VtM5e IS meant to be a direct follow-up to the past editions. That it is meant to continue the story and metaplot from before. So here, comparing it to past editions of VtM are much more warranted then in VtR.<br /> <br /> Intent, expectations, and context, are completely different, and therefore not comparable.<br /> <br /> ...also, Touchstones weren't a thing in VtR1e. They came later in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T18:10:33-07:00","id":1214858,"title":"","content":"VtR was absolutely intended as a &quot;reboot&quot; of VtM at the time. I remember those days, and WW in it's bonkers naivety thought everyone was going to be thrilled that VtM got its gehenna and jump on board their new game which promised no meta-plot and a plethora of other things a vocal minority had been demanding of them for a while. It was a huge misstep on WW's part and cost them their company.<br /> <br /> I'm on the side though in full favor of V5 making the rule changes it's making. Hunger dice are awesome, and they're gonna do well as Rage/Paradox/Banality dice. It's something that will mesh well in other systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T19:03:55-07:00","id":1214875,"title":"","content":"It may be better to identify the nWoD as an intended successor to the WoD (which didn\u2019t work), while CofD has finally walked away from WoD except for sharing some motifs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:07:56-07:00","id":1214889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214837#post1214837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which even then, I'd say it's still not comparable due to intent.<br /> <br /> VtR (and subsequently the rest of nWoD/CofD) was meant to be a brand new gameline separate from the original WoD. Inspired by it, sure, but still a different gameline. The gameline was not and has never been Vampire the Masquerade 4th Edition, it was Vampire the Requiem. So to expect it to be almost exactly the same as VtMRev or to be as a follow up to it I feel was not the right mindset to make.<br /> <br /> Conversely, VtM5e IS meant to be a direct follow-up to the past editions. That it is meant to continue the story and metaplot from before. So here, comparing it to past editions of VtM are much more warranted then in VtR.<br /> <br /> Intent, expectations, and context, are completely different, and therefore not comparable.<br /> <br /> ...also, Touchstones weren't a thing in VtR1e. They came later in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the touchstones thing is totally on me. I just recognized it as a Requiem thing, I didn't know it was new to those rules, too.<br /> <br /> Intent, though, doesn't matter with respect to how one feels about things of this nature. I'm worried Masquerade's rules, if not the meta-plot, have taken a very hard turn toward the whole reason I didn't continue with Requiem, which was too many things changed that I actually liked about the rules. The reorganization, renaming, the changes to &lt;insert line powers and functional groups&gt; were way too far from what I was happy with in cWoD, not the mention the relatively short cycles on the editions, even with Revised being* the longest, felt like it was all a cash grab** at the time, of which I am not accusing Paradox/White Wolf/whomever-the-overarching-company-is of doing. That's just the way it was for me then and the rules really worry me right now in a similar way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Approximately.<br /> **Opinion only, not an accusation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:04:09-07:00","id":1215128,"title":"","content":"I remember a number of times a specific topic came up in usenet groups, online forums, and mailing lists.<br /> <br /> &quot;What would you change if the game rebooted from scratch.&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of things in the nWoD lines seem to come directly from those discussions.<br /> <br /> I also do think one of the main issues was unavoidable. At the time, comics, cards, and gaming were riding a gravy train. A /lot/ of teens and young adults were hitting them and spending money on them. They thought they could do no wrong. The mindset was the same thing that blew Marvel comics into Bankrupcy.<br /> <br /> While splitting the fanbase into 'buying new product' and 'sticking with buying old stuff from used bookstores' hastened the end, I don't think it was actually avoidable.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:54:18-07:00","id":1215209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1214858#post1214858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtR was absolutely intended as a &quot;reboot&quot; of VtM at the time. I remember those days, and WW in it's bonkers naivety thought everyone was going to be thrilled that VtM got its gehenna and jump on board their new game which promised no meta-plot and a plethora of other things a vocal minority had been demanding of them for a while. It was a huge misstep on WW's part and cost them their company.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Bonkers naivety&quot; doesn't even approach the thing... I never understood how they even thought it'd turn out good. Like, take away the thing people loved and was heavily invested in many levels. Change it totally and give them back a product, that <i>slightly </i>resembles the old one, but 90% of it is totally different.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they'd all be happy about it, sure...<br /> <br /> I agree, a loud minority was also &quot;guilty&quot; pushing that. People, who don't like the thing (myself included, on occassion) are always louder than the silent majoriy who just like it and want to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Sure, the new thing will be everything some people wanted out of the thing, in comparison to the old thing. Also, the new thing will bring in some new people. Still, if people are liking something to the point the thing being wildly successful, that's probably for a reason...<br /> <br /> What I've seen in Hungary, that some people were quite enthusiastic about NWoD. Even I bought some of the books and honestly, quite liked the core, that gave something that WoD really lacked: tools for interesting human stories, that was a great idea. Still, most of the WoD-players there took a look, decided that it isn't the WoD they liked and continued to play the revised edition. As far as I know, that happened in most places, outside the US.<br /> <br /> Truly, one of the best ideas in the whole WoD soap opera over the years was reviving CWoD and continuing both lines. I'm happy WW made the decision of keeping it that way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:50:43-07:00","id":1216184,"title":"","content":"What is going on in this thread? Several discussions seem to be happening simultaneously:<br /> nWoD didn't fail in fact it thrives and continues to be very successful and the community is, in my experiance, very active and enthusiastic. CofD products have not taken a turn for the worst. <br /> <br /> I agree wit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a>: it is nice that both cWoD and CofD are being developed. They appeal to different people (or in the case of myself, i like CofD and I like the cWoD enough to be interested in its continued development) and they are very different which is a good thing. Different strokes for different folks. <br /> <br /> On the topic at hand, It appears that VtM5e is largely going to be compatible to legacy editions to a degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:15:47-07:00","id":1216302,"title":"","content":"nWoD killed old white wolf. It decimated their market share and reduced them to a shell. Even if you like the game system or setting there's no doubt what it caused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:17:32-07:00","id":1216390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216302#post1216302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD killed old white wolf. It decimated their market share and reduced them to a shell. Even if you like the game system or setting there's no doubt what it caused.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and yet the line still continues today, cultivating its own fanbase.<br /> <br /> If it was that disastrous, it wouldn't still exist. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:26:25-07:00","id":1216392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216184#post1216184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is going on in this thread? Several discussions seem to be happening simultaneously:<br /> nWoD didn't fail in fact it thrives and continues to be very successful and the community is, in my experiance, very active and enthusiastic. CofD products have not taken a turn for the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216302#post1216302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD killed old white wolf. It decimated their market share and reduced them to a shell. Even if you like the game system or setting there's no doubt what it caused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I think both of you are right and wrong at the same time.<br /> <br /> NWoD in itself didn't kill WW (there was a lot more circumstances in play) and yes, it has a substantial fanbase. On rpg terms, it's a sucessful rpg. However, it's undeniable, that it never got as big, especially outside the US, than WoD did (even now, just take a look at how many CWoD books OPP published since V20 and how many CofD books. That's not a coincidence, IMO). I'd argue, the concept itself which NWoD was built around made/makes it impossible and that it rejected a lot of things that made WoD's success possible. But on the other hand it was hindered with outward circumstances too and heavily.<br /> <br /> So, In my eyes, CofD isn't a bad gameline. I like a lot of it, though, overall, I'm more of a WoD fan, but the writers of CofD, both editions, made a lot of good material, that's undeniable. The line, as a whole, wasn't and isn't a failure and wasn't the sole cause of WW's downfall. However, it was a failure in comparison to WoD's success, for a lot of reasons and yes, that a big portion of the fanbase turned their backs on WW because of the killing off of CWoD was indeed a part of their long dive. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:57:36-07:00","id":1216402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216302#post1216302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD killed old white wolf. It decimated their market share and reduced them to a shell. Even if you like the game system or setting there's no doubt what it caused.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might have been the appearance, but that's not how things went down as I recall. We start with sales declining in the latter days of the Revised Editions for WoD. Naturally, our first instinct is to start planning a new edition, essentially a fourth edition, but then a discussion starts with the point that we've been talking all this time about Gehenna coming and how long can we draw it out and still feel like we're creating cool stuff. Next, we say &quot;But what comes after Gehenna?&quot;. Is it more of the same story but with resolved plot lines and fewer vampires? Something post-apocalyptic? Or a total reboot that keeps the cool aspects but cleans up a lot of the &quot;dangly parts&quot; from a decade-ish of world-building?<br /> <br /> The third option seemed to garner the most excitement from the creative teams, although none of these directions were anywhere near to being unanimously applauded. The intimidation factor of the &quot;wall of green marble&quot; driving away new customers was often cited as a reason to make more than a normal new edition's kind of changes. That wasn't just about the physical books, but was very much a metaphor for all of the various reasons we had been hearing for why it was hard to get into Revised. Along the way, it was decided to offer the storylines of this new WoD in novels and anthologies, and keep the game books free of the &quot;meta plot&quot; and so not have new events show up in them that affected the world and invalidated our previous books and players' games.<br /> <br /> The NWoD core and VtR first edition sold crazy big, as did the next couple of core books, but the supplements dropped back to the same level as the declining sales that had started the whole thing. Because of internal allocations of resources, the fiction books, which would have delivered the depth to the setting if we'd proceeded as planned, were dropped. So, we had no real way of getting those interesting storylines out there, and at this point it is hard to know if that would have helped anyway.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, nWoD did actually provide more time for us to keep trying to get sustainable sales again across the company, but the changing marketplace was more the factor we should have been dealing with at that time. Maybe, if we had gone for just a new edition again, we would have had the same or better sales than nWoD, but there were no indicators we had available that suggested that would be the case, and there's no way of knowing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T18:48:25-07:00","id":1216417,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> , thank you, that was a very interesting explanation and recalling of memories!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216402#post1216402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might have been the appearance, but that's not how things went down as I recall. We start with sales declining in the latter days of the Revised Editions for WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you tell if it was the natural &quot;end of an editon&quot; decline, or something out of the ordinary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Naturally, our first instinct is to start planning a new edition, essentially a fourth edition, but then a discussion starts with the point that we've been talking all this time about Gehenna coming and how long can we draw it out and still feel like we're creating cool stuff. </div> </div> </div>I'm not surprised at all. It's somewhat natural with creative types, to want to make something new instead of &quot;just continuing the same-old-same-old&quot;. Also, it was somewhat of a zeitgeist in the industry, I think, around that time. D&amp;D 4e and Shadowrun 4e also made big changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next, we say &quot;But what comes after Gehenna?&quot;. Is it more of the same story but with resolved plot lines and fewer vampires? Something post-apocalyptic? Or a total reboot that keeps the cool aspects but cleans up a lot of the &quot;dangly parts&quot; from a decade-ish of world-building? </div> </div> </div>There are two things I might make a remark off:<br /> <br /> 1. those &quot;dangly parts&quot; might have been a lot of the things the fans actually liked, unfortunately, at least regarding the fluff.<br /> <br /> 2. I think you were right, although. After the wind-up of Revised, a &quot;soft&quot; Gehenna would have been a letdown and a post-apocalyptic setting would have been completely different than the core assumptuion of WoD. I think the version of Gehenna WW seems to go for now is possibble now, because plenty of time have passed since and the 20ths also happened. People grew accustomed to the world not ending. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The third option seemed to garner the most excitement from the creative teams, although none of these directions were anywhere near to being unanimously applauded. </div> </div> </div>Again, not surprisingly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The intimidation factor of the &quot;wall of green marble&quot; driving away new customers was often cited as a reason to make more than a normal new edition's kind of changes. That wasn't just about the physical books, but was very much a metaphor for all of the various reasons we had been hearing for why it was hard to get into Revised. </div> </div> </div>That's a big conundrum with all old settings and gamelines, IMO. Though, I think the intimidation factor for new fans was always exaggerated. I got into WoD on the very tail end of Revised and wasn't intimidated, on the contrary, it was cool that there are plenty of things to read and that the world had that kind of depth. Same with FR and lately, with Shadowrun. Now, that's anecdotal evidence and I'm sure some people got turned off, because of the marble wall, but I believe that was a minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Along the way, it was decided to offer the storylines of this new WoD in novels and anthologies, and keep the game books free of the &quot;meta plot&quot; and so not have new events show up in them that affected the world and invalidated our previous books and players' games. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The NWoD core and VtR first edition sold crazy big, as did the next couple of core books, but the supplements dropped back to the same level as the declining sales that had started the whole thing. </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people bought them, out of curiosity and then decided that it wasn't for them. That was certainly what happened with me and Mage the Awakening. I just went back to Revised WoD and most of my acquaintances did the same. I hope it won't be the same with V5, though...<br /> <br /> Why the sales dropped in the first place is an interesting question and it could have a lot of answers and also a mix of multiple ones (most likely). Shift of culture, generational change, people grew tired, decline in the rpg market, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because of internal allocations of resources, the fiction books, which would have delivered the depth to the setting if we'd proceeded as planned, were dropped. So, we had no real way of getting those interesting storylines out there, </div> </div> </div>That's a shame, really, i liked Three Shades of Night a lot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and at this point it is hard to know if that would have helped anyway. </div> </div> </div>I believe stories in general, in some form, are necessary for getting really big, because it helps maintaining long-term interest from people through, well, storylines and relatable characters. People are getting invested in the story. I know it's always like that with me, regarding rpgs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, nWoD did actually provide more time for us to keep trying to get sustainable sales again across the company, but the changing marketplace was more the factor we should have been dealing with at that time. Maybe, if we had gone for just a new edition again, we would have had the same or better sales than nWoD, but there were no indicators we had available that suggested that would be the case, and there's no way of knowing now. </div> </div> </div>Thanks again, it was quite instructive!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T19:54:45-07:00","id":1216447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216417#post1216417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the sales dropped in the first place is an interesting question and it could have a lot of answers and also a mix of multiple ones (most likely). Shift of culture, generational change, people grew tired, decline in the rpg market, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just reading something about this, and it came about at the same time gamers' attentions were being split among table top, internet/mmo, CCGs, and video games. Not enough time for all of them, and face time was starting to go CCG heavy over table top RPG because it was easier and didn't require the whole group to play.<br /> <br /> Also, I would like to second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a>'s thank you to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> for the insight into the inner workings at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T21:38:08-07:00","id":1216487,"title":"","content":"I also would like to echo the comments of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6363_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6363\" data-vbnamecard=\"6363\">PM\u00e1rk</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a>. I only brought up the turbulence of the first few years of VtR and the rest of the CofD. I don't begrudge other players' choice in enjoying CofD (far from it). My only concern is that nu-WW's proclamation of revising the ruleset/metaplot when they announced the plan on the new edition. <br /> <br /> I did place my preorder for V5, however, my new concern is the plan on centralizing their publishing and distribution through Modiphius. To spend nearly as much on shipping as the price of the book itself, leaves me a little dubious on how much I will spend on the new system itself. I just hope that nu-WW plans on putting as much product as possible in book stores, because, if I have to spend that much money on shipping, let's just say that my V5 section of my gaming bookshelves will be quite lonely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T21:52:21-07:00","id":1216490,"title":"","content":"To me, who didnt play the WoD until it was getting close to its end, Classic and Chronicles seem like fighting over if Marvel or DC are better. Even I have my preference, but I wouldn't say one is trash compared to the other. If it wasn't for the fact that the Classic books were super easy to get 2nd hand, which was the only way my poor innercity group could afford them, I could very much see myself having had a preference for Chronicles. So I just find it silly to get into wars over this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T05:56:15-07:00","id":1216592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216402#post1216402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The NWoD core and VtR first edition sold crazy big.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Masquerade fans(like myself) certainly helped contribute to that as we all purchased a copy of Requiem expecting something quite different than what we got(not that THAT is a bad thing). I know every single person in my gaming group in the Bronx purchased a copy...and went right back to playing Masquerade shortly after.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-08-2018, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:23:36-07:00","id":1216605,"title":"","content":"Considering the massive bump in interest Bloodlines created, I definitely think ending VtM was a silly decision. We have the benefit of hindsight but I think the &quot;Time of Judgement&quot; should have been an edition. Nothing said gehenna would have occurred overnight. You could have gotten a ton of mileage out of it. It's easy to blame the economy and marketplace, but this is the era Paizo rise to power so there were still definitely tabletop RPG customers.<br /> <br /> Slim down, adjust print run sizes, white the licensing out a bit more. I know you were doing some of that (DA:Fae actually sold out its print run). I liked a bit of what nWoD did (the core book was great, CtL is vastly superior to CtD (but DA:Fae is still my fav)) but I truly believe that WW would have survived if it hadn't gone to nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:49:46-07:00","id":1216616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216605#post1216605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the massive bump in interest Bloodlines created, I definitely think ending VtM was a silly decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, we will never know. And hell, even Bloodlines--with another 6 months of polish, would've easily been one of the best selling games of the year, as opposed to the cult status it has today. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:10:40-07:00","id":1216657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216592#post1216592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of Masquerade fans(like myself) certainly helped contribute to that as we all purchased a copy of Requiem expecting something quite different than what we got(not that THAT is a bad thing). I know every single person in my gaming group in the Bronx purchased a copy...and went right back to playing Masquerade shortly after.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I, too, purchased VtR 1e when it first came out expecting one thing, but getting another. I also then returned back to VtM.<br /> <br /> I just hope that V5 doesn't do too much trashing of the previous 4 editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:07:35-07:00","id":1216744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216657#post1216657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I, too, purchased VtR 1e when it first came out expecting one thing, but getting another. I also then returned back to VtM.<br /> <br /> I just hope that V5 doesn't do too much trashing of the previous 4 editions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I felt a similar way about Requiem. It was pretty much Masquerade without the extensive history, mythos, and dramatic persona to draw upon. Not a bad thing, especially if you were new to WoD, but when we had a good chunk of the old vamp books already, Requiem just had little to offer on its own. We just mined it for the fluff and crunch we liked and continued on with Masquerade. Did the same for the other games. Lost was the only one that intrigued me enough to want to play on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T12:28:08-07:00","id":1216764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216744#post1216744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I felt a similar way about Requiem. It was pretty much Masquerade without the extensive history, mythos, and dramatic persona to draw upon. Not a bad thing, especially if you were new to WoD, but when we had a good chunk of the old vamp books already, Requiem just had little to offer on its own. We just mined it for the fluff and crunch we liked and continued on with Masquerade. Did the same for the other games. Lost was the only one that intrigued me enough to want to play on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, NWoD 1e, IMO, was the best, when it diverged from WoD.<br /> <br /> The blue book (or core) line was really great, one of my favorite rpg books and again, really added something that WoD lacked. I like Dreaming, but Lost was a totally different and equally great take on the concept of changelings. Hunter was everything I wanted out of the concept. Geist to me was far more interesting than Wraith.<br /> <br /> However, when it came to the big three... Requiem was just Masquerade without yeah, 90% of the fluff, without the history, the interconnectedness with the human world, the clans, the conspiracies and the signature characters and their stories and with a forced (at least it felt forced to me) notion of totally isolated cities. Werewolf, the same and without the environmentalism (and I actually like the environmentalism aspect of Apocalypse a lot, so I missed that too). Mage, the same, but with the whole unified Atlantis backstory slapped on and without the great connection into real-world traditions and phenomena Ascension had.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T14:26:15-07:00","id":1216811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216764#post1216764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truly, NWoD 1e, IMO, was the best, when it diverged from WoD.<br /> <br /> The blue book (or core) line was really great, one of my favorite rpg books and again, really added something that WoD lacked. I like Dreaming, but Lost was a totally different and equally great take on the concept of changelings. Hunter was everything I wanted out of the concept. Geist to me was far more interesting than Wraith.<br /> <br /> However, when it came to the big three... Requiem was just Masquerade without yeah, 90% of the fluff, without the history, the interconnectedness with the human world, the clans, the conspiracies and the signature characters and their stories and with a forced (at least it felt forced to me) notion of totally isolated cities. Werewolf, the same and without the environmentalism (and I actually like the environmentalism aspect of Apocalypse a lot, so I missed that too). Mage, the same, but with the whole unified Atlantis backstory slapped on and without the great connection into real-world traditions and phenomena Ascension had.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. It was the best when it deviated.<br /> <br /> That said, there's lots of things I liked about Forsaken. Much of werewolf nature felt far more mythical than Apocalypse. Like the Uratha clearly came off like they were half-spirit beings from the get go, there was less cringey elements involving kinfolk vs wolf-blooded, and some mutual aspects of the game were better spelled out. Even little things like how it feels to learn gifts, and that they become a part of ones nature, like sight or smell, were nice little touches.<br /> <br /> However, I didn't like how the whole of the spirit world was this vile Darwinistic nightmare. It fit the themes of Forsaken, but I wouldn't lift it whole cloth into Apocalypse. Though I loved the idea of the Uratha tribes having a mythical origin and purpose, they felt really bland, and even unnecessary in comparison to the Garou's (though the Garou tribes often became terribly stereotypical and static). And, at least to me, Forsaken paradoxically lacked the same emphasis on spirituality than Apocalypse. IDK how to describe it, because in many ways Forsaken's spirits came off better as animistic reflections of their physical counterparts. However, unlike Apocalypse, the spirit and the physical worlds didn't feel as necessary to each others existence. It was more like managing an ugly marriage neither side could escape. The nature of Uratha society came off to my group as lacking any personal spirituality too, outside of the Forsaken's relationship to Luna, and even then. Same with the Pure. Their relationship to spirits was more of an alliance of convenience than having reverence that even BSDs have for the Wyrm. Taking into account their relationship to the Shadow, it's not surprising. Uratha are more hunters of monsters like slayers in the Buffyverse. So, perhaps that's the point. I haven't read as many Forsaken books as Apocalypse, but I've heard the Uratha get better fleshed out in the supplements.<br /> <br /> As for the environmental aspects of Apocalypse, I did enjoy that too. The Garou were dealing with something real and not just evil cultists summoning demons for the sake of EVUL. However, especially in the early books, it came off as really hammy at times, and far too reflective of the industrial age and onward. The Wyrm, and the Triat as a whole, needed a lot more nuance.<br /> <br /> Moving on to Mage's decedent, I've only started reading Awakening in the last year or so. That whole Atlantis part of their cosmology really alienated me when I first heard about it. It does lack the scope and depth of Ascension, but there's still some really cool stuff on its pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 05-08-2018, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T15:15:38-07:00","id":1216826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216605#post1216605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the massive bump in interest Bloodlines created, I definitely think ending VtM was a silly decision. We have the benefit of hindsight but I think the &quot;Time of Judgement&quot; should have been an edition. Nothing said gehenna would have occurred overnight. You could have gotten a ton of mileage out of it. It's easy to blame the economy and marketplace, but this is the era Paizo rise to power so there were still definitely tabletop RPG customers.<br /> <br /> Slim down, adjust print run sizes, white the licensing out a bit more. I know you were doing some of that (DA:Fae actually sold out its print run). I liked a bit of what nWoD did (the core book was great, CtL is vastly superior to CtD (but DA:Fae is still my fav)) but I truly believe that WW would have survived if it hadn't gone to nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines was never a factor in anything that had to do with having our books sell more, and I think you are way overestimating its importance when it came out. It took years and years (and mods and patches) for it to achieve the cult status it has.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously, your opinion is your opinion. But for us, at that time, there was nothing silly in the decision - it was a necessity. There was not then nor is there now any actual data that suggests that WW could just have let things stay as they were and everything would have turned out all right or better than the course we chose. Reducing our releases meant reducing our income, which meant firing lots of our folks. Without those folks, we wouldn't have been able to cover all the aspects of the business, which means even less stuff published and less income. Rinse and repeat and the whole ship sinks. So really, no, it's not easy to blame the economy and marketplace - we've had years to look back on the situation and see that nothing short of changing our business model would have worked.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:00:13-07:00","id":1216837,"title":"","content":"I might add, the whole situation WW was back in the day is precisely why I never liked the Gehenna (and the other various apocalypses) as a literal end-of-the-World thing Revised has built it up to. The whole game line and the story was just cornered because of it and I get why NWoD felt a good idea back then, instead of postponing it intermittently, or going the Buffy/Supernatural route.<br /> <br /> I know and understand that for some people, the apocalypses were an integral part of the setting, that for them it was a story that really built up and needed a nice bow on the box, at the end. That it needed an end. I wasn't ever a part of that crowd and I'm so happy the 20ths proved that the WoD doesn't need it to work, as it wasn't the central part of it at the beginning and for a long time after. I'm also infinitely happy that WW has chosen a path with it that I'm finding really intriguing and that BJD was a very-very great ramp-up to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't know how much of it was the result of the ideas of OPP writers and the conversations here, when OPP started to gear up for their next edition of Vampire, but I'm grateful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T16:15:47-07:00","id":1216842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1216826#post1216826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloodlines was never a factor in anything that had to do with having our books sell more, and I think you are way overestimating its importance when it came out. It took years and years (and mods and patches) for it to achieve the cult status it has.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously, your opinion is your opinion. But for us, at that time, there was nothing silly in the decision - it was a necessity. There was not then nor is there now any actual data that suggests that WW could just have let things stay as they were and everything would have turned out all right or better than the course we chose. Reducing our releases meant reducing our income, which meant firing lots of our folks. Without those folks, we wouldn't have been able to cover all the aspects of the business, which means even less stuff published and less income. Rinse and repeat and the whole ship sinks. So really, no, it's not easy to blame the economy and marketplace - we've had years to look back on the situation and see that nothing short of changing our business model would have worked.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't blame y'all. The market changed for a host of reasons, and you had to publish or perish. Despite the salt that sadly exists between many fans of the Old and New WoD, you did what was best for the company both financially and creatively. A lot of the stuff I do like about Chronicles probably never would have been written up if not for that decision, and even though I mined it to enhance the old line, my games would have been poorer without them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T18:06:12-07:00","id":1216872,"title":"","content":"I am going to have to disagree. To you guys inside it may have seemed like the best course to take, but time has proven it wasn't. You're suggesting basically that WW's fall was inevitable. Ending the primary money maker to gamble everything on nWoD was a mistake. Would other things have been more or less successful? We'll never know, but it's the cWOD that people care about and live, it's the cWOD that has kept any value to the WW marquee so it could be bought by CCP and Paradox. I'm not saying nWoD is bad, but it's like if TSR had ditched Faerun so they could push and only support Thunder Rift (and splitting their market up was had killed TSR). <br /> <br /> There were ways to refresh VtM without killing it. Requiem could have even worked as a post gehenna VtM with a little bit of tweaking and the right marketing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:39:33-07:00","id":1217413,"title":"","content":"I can appreciate what Requiem has managed to accomplish but OWoD ending took most of the things I loved about Vampire away. Metaplot is what made the gameline engaging. Clans were evocative and their history was fascinating. I spent hours reading the books to find hidden secrets. Compared to the entire generic feel of Requiem where yes you could come up with a lot on your own but I'm not a professional writer so I could never make content as interesting. I bought a lot of the NWoD books but it never captured me like OWoD did. I look at how other RPG's like D&amp;D, Shadowrun, and others have managed to keep going throughout this time and I cant believe how the 2nd most popular(arguably) RPG company wasn't able to make it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T09:09:38-07:00","id":1217421,"title":"","content":"Please don't mistake why I've posting here: it's not to convince anyone to love VtR. Both WoD and CofD have a lot of great things to recommend about them, but they do appeal to different gaming styles and preferences. Mostly. As for why WoD would have had problems but not D&amp;D or Shadowrun, I'm pretty sure that we all know how D&amp;D lost its crown as industry leader and has now regained it, and my impression is that Shadowrun has had a fair number of ups and downs as well, in these intervening years. We've done our darndest to bring back WoD as we all enjoyed it with our Twentieth Anniversary lines, and now we all get to see if Vampire 5th can bring WoD into a new edition folks can get excited for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T14:17:07-07:00","id":1217493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1217421#post1217421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't mistake why I've posting here: it's not to convince anyone to love VtR. Both WoD and CofD have a lot of great things to recommend about them, but they do appeal to different gaming styles and preferences. Mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Requiem as I've always seen it, is a re-focusing on street/low-level play and a rejection of metaplot and big, driving conflicts. It is a kinda Greyhawk, compared to Masquerade's Forgotten Realms. It was always clear that a sizeable portion of the fanbase preferred that style, even during the original run of Masquerade. IMO, it was just a miscalculation, how big that portion exactly was. It was also more catered to people who didn't like the interconnectedness with the real world, either in the form of clans being tied to cultures or ethnicities and in the sense of bakstory in general. Problem is, those are actually big players in WoD's worldwide success, I believe. It's epic, it's a great story, it's interesting and it provides a lot of real-world connections which through people could feel, well, connected to the setting and story. For example, as a Hungarian, it was really fun to read the Revised Brujah and Gangrel books, with all the references to my country in the clan's history. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for why WoD would have had problems but not D&amp;D or Shadowrun, I'm pretty sure that we all know how D&amp;D lost its crown as industry leader and has now regained it, and my impression is that Shadowrun has had a fair number of ups and downs as well, in these intervening years. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I believe NWoD just doesn't catered to being as big a success as WoD was, due to the very founding principles of it, but it also had a very rough time in the industry for its run too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've done our darndest to bring back WoD as we all enjoyed it with our Twentieth Anniversary lines, and now we all get to see if Vampire 5th can bring WoD into a new edition folks can get excited for. </div> </div> </div>And again, I thank you for that! We could all be grateful that OPP proved that there is plenty of life in WoD and that there is a demand for new books. I'm very glad you brought it back to being an active IP and I'm glad CofD fans could keep their preferred games too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T14:48:53-07:00","id":1217502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1217493#post1217493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... It was also more catered to people who didn't like the interconnectedness with the real world, either in the form of clans being tied to cultures or ethnicities and in the sense of bakstory in general. Problem is, those are actually big players in WoD's worldwide success, I believe. It's epic, it's a great story, it's interesting and it provides a lot of real-world connections which through people could feel, well, connected to the setting and story. For example, as a Hungarian, it was really fun to read the Revised Brujah and Gangrel books, with all the references to my country in the clan's history. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it tho?<br /> I mean, with the Dark Eras, the bloodlines books, clanbooks, covenant books (individually and secret of the covenant), the ancient mysteries book, damnation city and danse macabre. I see a lot of interconnectedness with the real world. I see it far more than with masquerade actually.<br /> <br /> Hum... and then a thought strikes me. I've pretty much only read i think the revised core and V20 while reading a fair number on the Requiem line. So it stands to reason that for me the Requiem ''world'' feels more developped.<br /> And then perhaps the problem applies on the inverse too.<br /> I suddenly have the feeling that alot of peoples are comparing the Requiem 1ed corebook with everything written for Masquerade and then complaining that Requiem is less developped and offer less interconnectedness with the real world in comparison. <br /> <br /> Or i completely misunderstood what you meant with interconnectedness with the real world.<br /> <br /> All that said i wholly agree with the idea that both line are equally interesting and they are thus for their own reasons. Meaning, i'd play masquerade because i want to play in masquerades' world and i'd play requiem for what it offers as well. I dont really see a need to like one more than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T18:10:02-07:00","id":1217546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1211302-opp-vtm-5e-and-the-future?p=1217502#post1217502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it tho?<br /> I mean, with the Dark Eras, the bloodlines books, clanbooks, covenant books (individually and secret of the covenant), the ancient mysteries book, damnation city and danse macabre. I see a lot of interconnectedness with the real world. I see it far more than with masquerade actually.<br /> <br /> Hum... and then a thought strikes me. I've pretty much only read i think the revised core and V20 while reading a fair number on the Requiem line. So it stands to reason that for me the Requiem ''world'' feels more developped.<br /> And then perhaps the problem applies on the inverse too.<br /> I suddenly have the feeling that alot of peoples are comparing the Requiem 1ed corebook with everything written for Masquerade and then complaining that Requiem is less developped and offer less interconnectedness with the real world in comparison.<br /> <br /> Or i completely misunderstood what you meant with interconnectedness with the real world.<br /> <br /> All that said i wholly agree with the idea that both line are equally interesting and they are thus for their own reasons. Meaning, i'd play masquerade because i want to play in masquerades' world and i'd play requiem for what it offers as well. I dont really see a need to like one more than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you didn't misunderstand.<br /> <br /> Also yes, you are right that people got those impressions from the core books and that it's somewhat unfair to compare that to the entire length of WoD.<br /> <br /> <i>However</i>. WoD's interconnectedness is baked into the setting right from the start, from the core books, into the clans, into the history chapters, into the very workings of the game. It immediatelly gives people a lot of footholds and grasps to the setting that they could identify with. CofD added a lot of those things <i>later</i> in the form of the books you just listed and added them as <i>options</i>, as, almost, an afterthought and not as a story, not as a baseline.<br /> <br /> Also, the different groups connection to the real world was apparent even in the core books of WoD (even, if out of space and thus, necesity, they were stereotypical) and the clanbooks and so <i>expanded </i>on it. The CofD splats were pretty generic, conceptual things and added the connectedness only in the supplements and even then, they've kept it in a more vague form than WoD did. Honestly, even with the supplements, I've always felt that CofD kept itself a step back to the real world, in comparison to WoD. Like almost as if WoD received so much criticism from several circles for &quot;supernaturals being behind everything&quot; and &quot;stereotyping&quot; and even &quot;racism&quot; that the NWoD writers wanted to keep an arm's length. <br /> <br /> Also, CofD, while later it had periodical supplements and lately, the Dark Eras books, it never had the kind of intertwined, continual story-like connection to real-world history that WoD had. As I see it, WoD's take on this is &quot;let's see how the supernaturals shaped and got shaped by the things that happened and the world around them, <i>actively </i>and how the points line up to now&quot;, while CofD's is &quot;let's see how <i>specific</i> supernatural communities of a <i>specific </i>time period and geographical location looked out&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-10-2018, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:25:08-07:00","id":1218347,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that based on everything I've heard and read, that I'm going to stay with V20 as being the final edition and keep the metaplot as is. I'll evolve it to my groups but yeah, V20 is the end for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}